ate of in-\ndigenous people is generally below 30%, and intangible cultural\nheritage skills are at risk of interruption in inheritance. It is neces-\nsary to achieve a closed loop of ”protection - benefit - participation”\nthrough policy guidance.\n4.2 Model bottlenecks and optimization\nrecommendations\n4.2.1 International cooperation experience. The ”government-led +\ncommunity crowdfunding” model used by Eastern European coun-\ntries such as Bulgaria and Hungary for historical buildings preser-\nvation can provide institutional design references for Chongqing.\nTsyganov (2022) found that Bulgaria’s digital authorization   use static pictures to show Bombing site\ninstead of Scenically reproduce the noise of a group refuge and\nkerosene lamp lighting.\n2.4.3 Fragmented User Experience in Using Services. When using\nAR guides, visitors need to wait for an average of 2.7 seconds (that\nis, launching mobile games require an average of 2.7 seconds to\n553\x0cDSAI 2025, May 23–25, 2025, Wuhan, China Yue Yang and Bin Chen\nFigure 6: Digital Twin System for Chongqing Red Culture in Vernacular Dwellings. Photograph by Yue Yang.\nTable 2: Core Metrics of Digital Preservation and Tourism Development.\nCase Name Technology Application Historical\nCognition\nImprovement\nEEG Positive Signal\nChange\nAverage\nDwell Time\nRepeat\nVisit\nRate\nData Source\nHuangshan Site\nCluster\nVR Panorama +\nDocument Database\n+58% -35% (Excessive\nCommercialization)\n45 mins →\n67 mins\n12% →\n30%\n2025-2031\nGlobal\nImmersive\nAttraction\nMarket Report\nHongyan 1949\nExperience Center\nDynamic Narrative\nSystem (Bombing\nAlarms)\n+53% -40% (Cafe\nImplantation)\n27 mins →\n49 mins\n15% →\n33%\nChongqing\nDaily\nCiqikou Ancient\nTown\nAR Guidance + Haptic\nGloves\n+49% -28% (Commercial\nStreet Diversion)\n38 mins →\n60 mins\n18% →\n36%\nPeople’s Net\nShanchengxiang\nAir-Raid Shelter\nMulti-Sensory\nIntegration (Olfactory +\nTemp)\n+67% -18% (Moderate\nScene Implantation)\n33 mins →\n55 mins