e’s Posts and Telecommunications Press.\n[9] Tsyganov, M. (2022). Digital preservation of Balkan architectural heritage: Techni-\ncal innovations and community engagement. Sofia: Balkan Heritage Press. ISBN\n978-954-2976-22-1.\n557  standard of Digital Protection of Intangible Cultural\nHeritage (2023) [3].It reconstructs historical scene such as bomb-\ning scene with temporal-space information. Historical knowledge\nretention rate has been increased by 58%.\n1.2.3 Industrial Convergence. A digital twin platform for home-\nstay in rural tourism. Homestay price increased 126% (200 →480\nCNY/night), and online cultural revenue accounted for 41% of total\nincome (Ciqikou Ancient Town case).\n2 Current Status of Technologies for Data\nAcquisition and Modeling\n2.1 Data Acquisition and Modeling\nTechnologies\n2.1.1 3D Laser Scanning. FARO Focus S350 realizes millimeter-\nlevel point cloud modeling. The thermal map of structural damage\nis generated with an average error margin <0.5% (Table 1) and meets\nthe requirements of heritage monitoring by UNESCO[4].\n2.1.2 Drone Oblique Photography. Drone Oblique Photography\nImages acquired from the air with 50-150m height cover multi-angle\nviews (Figure 4). The textured 3D model is generated by Context\nCapture software based on the stitching of images. The decay con-\ndition of buildings can be identified, for example, the area of wood\ndarkening suggests corrosion. Based on GIS software, the spatial\nFigure 4: Aerial Photography of Peng’s Traditional Dwelling\nby UA V. Photograph by Yue Yang.\ndistribution of buildings can be analyzed. The model is not only the\nrepresentation of the appearance of buildings, but also the reflection\nof the material condition through the color of the buildings, for ex-\nample, the area of wood darkening represents the risk of corrosion\n(Figure 5)[5]. Finally, based on the electronic map technology (GIS),\nthe scattered 3D models are aggregated into spatial distribution\nmaps. The building density, the age distribution, and other impor-\ntant data are intuitively displayed by the map, which provides a\nscientific basis for the planning of heritage conservation[6].\n2.1.3 Dynamic data  \n\nStatement: Rural internet infrastructure has been discussed.\n\nTask:\nYou are a data auditor and need to determine if this statement is correct. Evaluate this statement strictly based on the provided background information. Do not use external knowledge.\n\nInstructions:\n- Output only a single digit: 5 or 1, 5 for True, 1 for False.\n- Do not include any explanation, punctuation, or extra text.\n\nYour output:'}], 'model': 'deepseek-reasoner', 'stream': False}}
