2026-05-28 03:12:33,051 - openai._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-c1384c40-b29a-4d31-ac5b-c2d979baa507', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': '\nContext:  interactive experience.\n2.3 User Experience Evaluation System\n2.3.1 Multimodal Interaction Testing. Tobii Pro eye tracker and\nEmotiv EEG device, the distribution of visitor’s attention and the\nemotion of visitors in VR scenario are quantified. The data show\nthat the historical cognition of visitors increased by 53% after the\nimplementation of dynamic narrative system, and the excessive\ncommercial operation would decrease the number of EEG positive\nsignals by 40%[7](Table 2).\n2.3.2 A/B Testing Optimization. Compared with traditional exhibi-\ntion, VR exhibition hall extended average stay time for 22 minutes\nand elevated repeat visitation rate by 18% (Table 2).\n2.4 Challenges in Digital Application\n2.4.1 Disparity between Urban and Rural Areas in Application of\nTechnology. There are notable disparities in digital preservation im-\nplementation between urban and rural areas of Chongqing. LOD400\nmodeling precision is adopted for projects in the central urban dis-\ntricts where all architectural ornaments such as window and door\ncarvings can be depicted. In comparison, modeling precision of\ncounty-level projects is restricted to LOD200 models that only re-\ntain basic outlines of buildings, and data interoperability rate is\nbelow 30%. As analyzed in 2023 China Rural Internet Development\nReport [ 8], r technical challenges that rural areas are facing are\nsummarized as follows: (1) point cloud data transmission failure\nrate in rural areas is as high as 18.7% (vs 2.3% in the urban cores)\n(2) although digital technologies can reduce surveying errors by\n92%, when using advanced methods, cost of modeling per building\nis 3-5 times higher than traditional methods (Table 3).\n2.4.2 Fragmented Scenarios in War Time. 85% of digital exhibitions\nonly passively show building exterior and wartime timeline but\nlack recreation of wartime life. For instance, when exhibiting bomb\nshelter, most cases only   use static pictures to show Bombing site\ninstead of Scenically reproduce the noise of a group refuge and\nkerosene lamp lighting.\n2.4.3 Fragmented User Experience in Using Services. When using\nAR guides, visitors need to wait for an average of 2.7 seconds (that\nis, launching mobile games require an average of 2.7 seconds to\n553\x0cDSAI 2025, May 23–25, 2025, Wuhan, China Yue Yang and Bin Chen\nFigure 6: Digital Twin System for Chongqing Red Culture in Vernacular Dwellings. Photograph by Yue Yang.\nTable 2: Core Metrics of Digital Preservation and Tourism Development.\nCase Name Technology Application Historical\nCognition\nImprovement\nEEG Positive Signal\nChange\nAverage\nDwell Time\nRepeat\nVisit\nRate\nData Source\nHuangshan Site\nCluster\nVR Panorama +\nDocument Database\n+58% -35% (Excessive\nCommercialization)\n45 mins →\n67 mins\n12% →\n30%\n2025-2031\nGlobal\nImmersive\nAttraction\nMarket Report\nHongyan 1949\nExperience Center\nDynamic Narrative\nSystem (Bombing\nAlarms)\n+53% -40% (Cafe\nImplantation)\n27 mins →\n49 mins\n15% →\n33%\nChongqing\nDaily\nCiqikou Ancient\nTown\nAR Guidance + Haptic\nGloves\n+49% -28% (Commercial\nStreet Diversion)\n38 mins →\n60 mins\n18% →\n36%\nPeople’s Net\nShanchengxiang\nAir-Raid Shelter\nMulti-Sensory\nIntegration (Olfactory +\nTemp)\n+67% -18% (Moderate\nScene Implantation)\n33 mins →\n55 mins\n21% →\n39%\nAuthor’s\nResearch\nTable 3: Cost-Effectiveness Comparison of Heritage Modeling Technologies.\nTechnology Type Costper Building (10k\nCNY)\nError Rate Data Acquisition\nTimeframe\nApplicable Scenarios\nTotal Station Surveying 0.8-1.2 2.3% 7-10 days General Cultural Heritage Sites\n3D Laser Scanning 3.5-5.0 0.5% 1-2 days Key Protected Heritage Buildings\nUA V Oblique Photography 1.2-2.0 1.8% 3-5 days Large-Scale Archaeological Sites\nload) and then experience the service. However, only 5% of venues\nprovide haptic devices, and therefore visitors are unable to feel\nshockwaves or scorched earth smells at Bombing site.\n3 Localized Practice of the Graded Protection\nFramework for Vernacular Dwellings\nBased on implementation of 3D laser scanning, virtual reality (VR),\nand big data analysis, this study collected architectural data and\ncompared architectural data of representative Chongqing Red Cul-\nture vernacular dwellings, and further proposed the collaborative\npractice of ”Graded Protection-Living Inheritance-Digital Twin. ”\nThe case study of   Digital Preservation of Chongqing Red Culture and Tourism\nResource Development in Bayu Traditional Dwellings\nYue Yang∗\nChongqing Institute of Engineering\nChongqing, China\n376521977@qq.com\nBin Chen\nChongqing Institute of Engineering\nChongqing, China\n149209173@qq.com\nAbstract\nAs the wartime capital of the Anti-Japanese War, Bayu area owns\ntraditional dwellings with wartime culture and architectural wis-\ndom left in. Focusing on the Chongqing Red Culture heritage, this\npaper explores digital representation approaches and tourism de-\nvelopment paths of Bayu traditional dwellings through field survey\nand digital technology analysis. Based on 3D laser scanning, VR\n(Virtual Reality) and big data, we collect architectural data and\nconduct comparative analysis on Typical Cases such as Huangshan\nAnti-Japanese War Site Cluster and Liziba War Relics Park. The\nmain results are as follows: (1) Digital technology can improve\narchitectural data collection accuracy (error rate <0.5%) and visi-\ntors’ immersion in virtual experience (the VR stay rate has been\nincreased by 40%); (2) Existing development models have the fol-\nlowing problems: too much functional replacement and lack of\ntechnical specifications; (3) A new framework of “graded protection-\nliving inheritance-digital twin” is proposed. Under the support of\nAR (Augmented Reality) guided tour and metaverse scenario, the\nframework develops dynamic narrative system (e.g. reconstruc-\ntion of bombing scene) under the standard of Digital Protection\nof Intangible Cultural Heritage (2023) [ 3] and improves historical\nknowledge retention rate by 58%. Case studies show that, compared\nwith traditional methods, this framework can increase tourism rev-\nenue by 18%-25% and reduce restoration cost by 30%. This research\nprovides theoretical basis and reference for the sustainable use of\nChongqing Red Culture heritage.\nCCS Concepts\n• Applied computing →Arts and humanities; Architecture (build-\nings).\nKeywords\nTraditional dwellings, Chongqing Red Culture, Digital Preservation,\nCultural-Tourism Integration, digital twin technology\nACM Reference Format:\nYue Yang and Bin Chen. 2025.  \n\nStatement: Indigenous people (local residents) participant in Traditional exhibition methods\n\nTask:\nYou are a data auditor and need to determine if this statement is correct. Evaluate this statement strictly based on the provided background information. Do not use external knowledge.\n\nInstructions:\n- Output only a single digit: 5 or 1, 5 for True, 1 for False.\n- Do not include any explanation, punctuation, or extra text.\n\nYour output:'}], 'model': 'deepseek-reasoner', 'stream': False}}
