 the\nvirtual menu also provided instructions on activating and performing each action.Figure 3\nshows the four types of actions provided by the virtual menu in VR.\nThanks to the motion tracking system and sensors embedded in Oculus Quest, navigation\nin virtual environments was similar to walking and viewing in the real world.   treatment group where the immersive VR training system was\nimplemented and a control group where an excavation health and safety manual was used.\nParticipants answered a pre-training questionnaire that collected demographic information\nand prior experience in construction, excavation and safety training. Also, the questionnaire\nmeasured participants’ excavation safety knowledge and self-efficacy.\nFor the treatment group (VR), participants received instructions and health and safety\ninduction about VR and the use of Oculus Quest and undertook VR tutorials in the office\nscenario. When participants were comfortable with VR, they proceeded to Site A where\ntraining took place. In this case, the pre-training practical assessment at Site A and post-\ntraining practical assessment at Site B were skipped. After completing training, participants\nexited VR and answered a post-training questionnaire about their excavation safety\nknowledge and self-efficacy.\nParticipants in the controlgroup (Manual) received health  \n\nStatement: Immersive VR training system adopt Oculus Quest wireless controllers\n\nTask:\nYou are a data auditor and need to determine if this statement is correct. Evaluate this statement strictly based on the provided background information. Do not use external knowledge.\n\nInstructions:\n- Output only a single digit: 5 or 1, 5 for True, 1 for False.\n- Do not include any explanation, punctuation, or extra text.\n\nYour output:'}], 'model': 'deepseek-reasoner', 'stream': False}}
