earch oriented to the needs of modern human–computer interaction. To fill this gap, this paper proposes and realizes The Wonderful Journey Based on Baduanjin (TWJB), a gamified rehabilitation system that integrates traditional culture and intelligent interaction technology.   guidance, gamified rewards, and cultural storytelling to enhance both rehabilitation out-\ncomes and user interest in the intangible cultural heritage of Baduanjin.\nAt the core of TWJB is a feedback-driven interaction loop. The user’s movement is continuously tracked via skeletal joint data, which feeds into a motion recognition module to determine real-time action similarity scores. Based on these results, the virtual NPC adjusts its response: if the action is correct, cultural rewards and level progression are granted; if incorrect, the NPC replays a slowed-down demonstra-\ntion and provides semantic corrections. This interaction loop ensures that user performance directly influences system behavior, enabling adaptive and personalized training.\n3.2.1. Virtual image\nIn the TWJB system, this study designed two avatars: the user avatar and the accompanying avatar (NPC ’Liu Miaozhen’).\nFig. 3. Eight-duanjin movement guidance.\n(1) User  \n\nStatement: The Wonderful Journey Based on Baduanjin (TWJB) system adopt Cascadeur\n\nTask:\nYou are a data auditor and need to determine if this statement is correct. Evaluate this statement strictly based on the provided background information. Do not use external knowledge.\n\nInstructions:\n- Output only a single digit: 5 or 1, 5 for True, 1 for False.\n- Do not include any explanation, punctuation, or extra text.\n\nYour output:'}], 'model': 'deepseek-reasoner', 'stream': False}}
