earch oriented to the needs of modern human–computer interaction. To fill this gap, this paper proposes and realizes The Wonderful Journey Based on Baduanjin (TWJB), a gamified rehabilitation system that integrates traditional culture and intelligent interaction technology.   The system is based on somatosensory recognition devices and constructs a reha-\nbilitation interaction process centered on avatar guidance, immersive plot advancement, and knowledge card feedback through an immersive designed interaction experience. This study aims to enhance patients’ rehabilitation motivation, interaction experience and cultural identity, and to transform users from passive receivers to active participants. In order to systematically support the standard presentation and al-\ngorithmic training of Baduanjin movements, this paper also organizes and constructs a movement animation data repository containing the eight styles of movements, realizes the unified mapping of standard movement keyframes, movement semantics and voice commands, and enriches the system’s content depth and expandability.\nIn this paper, a controlled experiment with 78 subjects was con-\nducted to evaluate the comprehensive effect of the TWJB system in the dimensions  \n\nStatement: The Wonderful Journey Based on Baduanjin (TWJB) system adopt Baduanjin movement instructions\n\nTask:\nYou are a data auditor and need to determine if this statement is correct. Evaluate this statement strictly based on the provided background information. Do not use external knowledge.\n\nInstructions:\n- Output only a single digit: 5 or 1, 5 for True, 1 for False.\n- Do not include any explanation, punctuation, or extra text.\n\nYour output:'}], 'model': 'deepseek-reasoner', 'stream': False}}
