his interaction loop ensures that user performance directly influences system behavior, enabling adaptive and personalized training.\n3.2.1. Virtual image\nIn the TWJB system, this study designed two avatars: the user avatar and the accompanying avatar (NPC ’Liu Miaozhen’).\nFig. 3. Eight-duanjin movement guidance.\n(1) User   audio. Given the unique nature of each movement, the system offers personalized feedback aligned with the user’s real-\ntime performance and progress. The historical background and health-\nrelated knowledge of Baduanjin are embedded into the interaction flow. As users engage in training, the virtual guide ‘‘Liu Miaozhen’’ leads them through the eight forms. After each completed movement, the system evaluates performance, delivers feedback, and issues related cul-\ntural knowledge cards to promote learning and motivation. The overall structure of this training-interaction–feedback process is illustrated in Fig. 1.\nTo support user interaction, the system establishes a dual-character model consisting of a real-time user avatar and a virtual NPC. The avatar mirrors user movements via skeletal tracking, while the NPC ‘‘Liu Miaozhen’’ performs multiple functions such as motion demonstra-\ntion, voice instruction, and cultural narration.  \n\nStatement: Traditional text and graphic training methods is constrained by Lagging feedback\n\nTask:\nYou are a data auditor and need to determine if this statement is correct. Evaluate this statement strictly based on the provided background information. Do not use external knowledge.\n\nInstructions:\n- Output only a single digit: 5 or 1, 5 for True, 1 for False.\n- Do not include any explanation, punctuation, or extra text.\n\nYour output:'}], 'model': 'deepseek-reasoner', 'stream': False}}
