y, and immersive interaction. A closed-loop logic of ‘‘action–feedback–culture’’ is embedded throughout the system design.\n3.1. Design concept and material\nAccording to the findings from the preliminary survey, virtual char-\nacters and participatory interaction play critical roles in rehabilitation engagement. Gamified interaction was shown to enhance entertainment and motivation. Therefore, the TWJB   of interactive experience, knowledge acquisition and functional recovery, and to explore its practical value under the dual goals of digital rehabilitation and cultural dissemination. The innova-\ntive contributions of this study are mainly reflected in the following three points:\n(1) Proposing a gamified rehabilitation system design method that integrates virtualized body, embodied interaction and the cultural el-\nements of Baduanjin, which expands the digital interactive expres-\nsion paths of non-heritage content while improving the compliance of rehabilitation;\n(2) A multimodal perception mechanism based on user movement and voice feedback is constructed to achieve automatic assessment and personalized guidance on the accuracy and completion of rehabilitation movements;\n(3) Constructed a standardized Baduanjin animation asset library tailored for rehabilitation scenarios, which facilitates the normative representation of intangible cultural heritage and supports the integra-\ntion of motion recognition  \n\nStatement: Healthy adult volunteers participant in TWJB system (gamified virtual rehabilitation system)\n\nTask:\nYou are a data auditor and need to determine if this statement is correct. Evaluate this statement strictly based on the provided background information. Do not use external knowledge.\n\nInstructions:\n- Output only a single digit: 5 or 1, 5 for True, 1 for False.\n- Do not include any explanation, punctuation, or extra text.\n\nYour output:'}], 'model': 'deepseek-reasoner', 'stream': False}}
