ce, user experience, and cultural awareness, a between-subjects user study was conducted in a university laboratory. Two cohorts of participants were recruited to compare the TWJB system — based on somatosensory interaction — with a traditional   application.\n2.2. Gamification experience of intangible cultural heritage\nGamification experience significantly improves user engagement and knowledge retention by integrating game design elements (e.g.,\ntask challenges, point rewards, interactive feedback) into non-game scenarios (e.g., education, cultural dissemination). In intangible cul-\ntural heritage (ICH) preservation, technologies such as virtual reality (VR) and augmented reality (AR) provide users with immersive ex-\nperiences through 3D visualization and interactive modes, breaking through the limitations of traditional passive learning [12,13]. Stud-\nies have shown that VR technology can build virtual museums or interactive narrative scenes to enhance users’ intuitive perception of cultural knowledge [14,15]. For example, VR-based interactive designs can effectively enhance users’ awareness of cultural heritage [16,17]. In addition, mixed reality (MR) technology further promotes users’ active participation in cultural heritage by combining gamification mechanisms [18]. These technologies not  \n\nStatement: Cultural historical background is transferred by Knowledge quiz game\n\nTask:\nYou are a data auditor and need to determine if this statement is correct. Evaluate this statement strictly based on the provided background information. Do not use external knowledge.\n\nInstructions:\n- Output only a single digit: 5 or 1, 5 for True, 1 for False.\n- Do not include any explanation, punctuation, or extra text.\n\nYour output:'}], 'model': 'deepseek-reasoner', 'stream': False}}
